WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.164
Your first week has one goal: build a

00:00:03.164 --> 00:00:05.977
record you can actually use. Start small, and

00:00:05.977 --> 00:00:08.439
keep the detail while it is fresh.

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:12.240
Check your profile and unit membership first. Review

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.640
the visibility setting whenever you create a record.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.041
Your role and membership determine which team views

00:00:19.041 --> 00:00:20.316
you can access.

00:00:20.716 --> 00:00:23.846
Log one real outcome from your day. Include

00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:26.976
what you did, how much you completed, and

00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:30.106
why it mattered. Review the fields and save

00:00:30.106 --> 00:00:30.889
the activity.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:34.490
If you missed context, edit the record. Then

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.692
choose one measurable goal. Use a target with

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:40.893
a clear unit, so progress tells you something

00:00:40.893 --> 00:00:41.293
useful.

00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:44.465
At the end of the week, review your

00:00:44.465 --> 00:00:47.238
records for missing detail and check the reporting

00:00:47.238 --> 00:00:50.010
period. Open the source behind a figure before

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.050
relying on it.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.447
Capture while the detail is fresh. Check what

00:00:54.447 --> 00:00:57.445
you saved. Review the week. That is enough

00:00:57.445 --> 00:00:59.693
to make your first week useful.
